{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"CLSA-2026-1792072825","published":"2026-10-15T14:00:37Z","modified":"2026-10-26T09:32:02.917907183Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-106568","CVE-2026-109263","CVE-2026-109275"],"summary":"Fix CVE(s): CVE-2026-106568, CVE-2026-109263, CVE-2026-109275","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: infinite loop on circular parameter entities\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-106568.patch: check entity values for both\n       '%' and '&' references in ValidateEntities() so circular parameter\n       entity declarations are rejected in ParseInternalDoctype() in\n       magick/xml-tree.c\n     - CVE-2026-106568\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory leak in the YUV encoder\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-109263.patch: destroy the luma image when the\n       chroma ResizeImage() fails and destroy the chroma image after the\n       encoding loop in WriteYUVImage() in coders/yuv.c\n     - CVE-2026-109263\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: PostScript code injection through the font name\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-109275.patch: only pass font names made of\n       alphanumerics, '-', '_' and '.' to the PostScript renderer in\n       RenderPostscript() in magick/annotate.c\n     - CVE-2026-109275","affected":[{"package":{"name":"imagemagick","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:16.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/imagemagick?distro=ubuntu-16.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8:6.8.9.9-7ubuntu5.17+tuxcare.els65"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu16.04els/CLSA-2026-1792072825.json"}},{"package":{"name":"imagemagick-6.q16","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:16.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/imagemagick-6.q16?distro=ubuntu-16.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"8:6.8.9.9-7ubuntu5.17+tuxcare.els65"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu16.04els/CLSA-2026-1792072825.json"}},{"package":{"name":"imagemag